{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsnppxNkizvTPrhGBdBZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"With the Keychain step out of the way, the run reaches OpenRouter and fails only on the dummy key. I'll write ANSWER.md and check the final diff."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":914,"cache_read_input_tokens":50343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":914},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69cb1ba0-5b4a-44ed-a6f2-d183ed56b688","uuid":"115efaf5-2e98-47d0-beb1-5a6769f7331d","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:00:33.675Z","request_id":"req_011CgsnppmDYswVgeBFJcgJf"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsnppxNkizvTPrhGBdBZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017FciNCj4H4ppG176Lkacim","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-z7T18m/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why every run-vibe.sh run exits in about a second\n\n**Cause:** at startup Mistral Vibe looks up `MISTRAL_API_KEY` in the macOS Keychain by running\n`/usr/bin/security`. The run's `agent.sb` sandbox denies `process-exec` for that binary, so the exec fails with\n`PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted: '/usr/bin/security'`. Vibe's keyring code\n(`vibe/utils/keyring.py`, `_run_security`) only wraps `FileNotFoundError`, so the `PermissionError` is not turned\ninto a handled error and Vibe exits with status 2 before it makes any model call. `logs/last-run.err` shows exactly\nthis.\n\nVibe asks for `MISTRAL_API_KEY` even though the configured provider is OpenRouter, which reads `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`\nfrom the environment. The OpenRouter key was never the problem: `resolve_api_key(\"OPENROUTER_API_KEY\")` returns\nthe env value without touching the Keychain.\n\n**Reproduced:** under the same `agent.sb` profile, `resolve_api_key(\"MISTRAL_API_KEY\")` raises the same\n`PermissionError`, and `resolve_api_key(\"OPENROUTER_API_KEY\")` succeeds.\n\n**Fix:** `run-vibe.sh` now passes `VIBE_TEST_DISABLE_KEYRING=1` into the sandboxed environment. Vibe's keyring\nmodule honours this switch: `get_api_key_from_keyring` returns `None` without calling `security`. I checked that\n`MISTRAL_API_KEY` then resolves to `None` under the sandbox with no error. I did not loosen `agent.sb`, so the\nKeychain and the real home directory are still unreachable.\n\n**Verification:** with a placeholder `OPENROUTER_API_KEY=dummy-test-key`, the script now gets past startup and fails\nonly at OpenRouter's auth check (`Invalid API key (from env var OPENROUTER_API_KEY)`, exit 1). Startup is fixed. I did\nnot run a real prompt, because `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is not set in the shell I worked in. With your real key set,\n`./run-vibe.sh \"say hi\" /tmp/x` should now run normally.\n\n**Notes:**\n- The stderr text `Reading API keys from the macOS Keychain (...)` in the old log does not appear in the installed\n  Vibe 3.1.0 source. The traceback logic matches, so the log probably came from a slightly different build. The fix\n  holds either way, because the switch is checked before any Keychain read.\n- `VIBE_TEST_DISABLE_KEYRING` is a test-oriented name. It is the only switch I found that stops the Keychain read\n  without changing the installed package or the sandbox. If Vibe is upgraded, check that it still honours it.\n- Alternatives I rejected: allowing `/usr/bin/security` in `agent.sb` (widens the sandbox), or setting a dummy\n  `MISTRAL_API_KEY` (hacky, and it could be sent somewhere). Fixing `_run_security` in the installed package would\n  be the upstream fix, but it is outside this directory.\n- `logs/last-run.out` and `logs/last-run.err` now hold the output of the placeholder-key test run.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":914,"cache_read_input_tokens":50343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":914},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69cb1ba0-5b4a-44ed-a6f2-d183ed56b688","uuid":"0ac55e81-2d3f-45df-9377-f26b21530dea","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:00:38.716Z","request_id":"req_011CgsnppmDYswVgeBFJcgJf","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017FciNCj4H4ppG176Lkacim":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-z7T18m/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why every run-vibe.sh run exits in about a second\n\n**Cause:** at startup Mistral Vibe looks up `MISTRAL_API_KEY` in the macOS Keychain by running\n`/usr/bin/security`. The run's `agent.sb` sandbox denies `process-exec` for that binary, so the exec fails with\n`PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted: '/usr/bin/security'`. Vibe's keyring code\n(`vibe/utils/keyring.py`, `_run_security`) only wraps `FileNotFoundError`, so the `PermissionError` is not turned\ninto a handled error and Vibe exits with status 2 before it makes any model call. `logs/last-run.err` shows exactly\nthis.\n\nVibe asks for `MISTRAL_API_KEY` even though the configured provider is OpenRouter, which reads `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`\nfrom the environment. The OpenRouter key was never the problem: `resolve_api_key(\"OPENROUTER_API_KEY\")` returns\nthe env value without touching the Keychain.\n\n**Reproduced:** under the same `agent.sb` profile, `resolve_api_key(\"MISTRAL_API_KEY\")` raises the same\n`PermissionError`, and `resolve_api_key(\"OPENROUTER_API_KEY\")` succeeds.\n\n**Fix:** `run-vibe.sh` now passes `VIBE_TEST_DISABLE_KEYRING=1` into the sandboxed environment. Vibe's keyring\nmodule honours this switch: `get_api_key_from_keyring` returns `None` without calling `security`. I checked that\n`MISTRAL_API_KEY` then resolves to `None` under the sandbox with no error. I did not loosen `agent.sb`, so the\nKeychain and the real home directory are still unreachable.\n\n**Verification:** with a placeholder `OPENROUTER_API_KEY=dummy-test-key`, the script now gets past startup and fails\nonly at OpenRouter's auth check (`Invalid API key (from env var OPENROUTER_API_KEY)`, exit 1). Startup is fixed. I did\nnot run a real prompt, because `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is not set in the shell I worked in. With your real key set,\n`./run-vibe.sh \"say hi\" /tmp/x` should now run normally.\n\n**Notes:**\n- The stderr text `Reading API keys from the macOS Keychain (...)` in the old log does not appear in the installed\n  Vibe 3.1.0 source. The traceback logic matches, so the log probably came from a slightly different build. The fix\n  holds either way, because the switch is checked before any Keychain read.\n- `VIBE_TEST_DISABLE_KEYRING` is a test-oriented name. It is the only switch I found that stops the Keychain read\n  without changing the installed package or the sandbox. If Vibe is upgraded, check that it still honours it.\n- Alternatives I rejected: allowing `/usr/bin/security` in `agent.sb` (widens the sandbox), or setting a dummy\n  `MISTRAL_API_KEY` (hacky, and it could be sent somewhere). Fixing `_run_security` in the installed package would\n  be the upstream fix, but it is outside this directory.\n- `logs/last-run.out` and `logs/last-run.err` now hold the output of the placeholder-key test run.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017FciNCj4H4ppG176Lkacim","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /private/tmp/h-z7T18m/ANSWER.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69cb1ba0-5b4a-44ed-a6f2-d183ed56b688","uuid":"7cd248a6-18b3-4465-bf24-b2ea9e3fa076","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:00:38.737Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/private/tmp/h-z7T18m/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why every run-vibe.sh run exits in about a second\n\n**Cause:** at startup Mistral Vibe looks up `MISTRAL_API_KEY` in the macOS Keychain by running\n`/usr/bin/security`. The run's `agent.sb` sandbox denies `process-exec` for that binary, so the exec fails with\n`PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted: '/usr/bin/security'`. Vibe's keyring code\n(`vibe/utils/keyring.py`, `_run_security`) only wraps `FileNotFoundError`, so the `PermissionError` is not turned\ninto a handled error and Vibe exits with status 2 before it makes any model call. `logs/last-run.err` shows exactly\nthis.\n\nVibe asks for `MISTRAL_API_KEY` even though the configured provider is OpenRouter, which reads `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`\nfrom the environment. The OpenRouter key was never the problem: `resolve_api_key(\"OPENROUTER_API_KEY\")` returns\nthe env value without touching the Keychain.\n\n**Reproduced:** under the same `agent.sb` profile, `resolve_api_key(\"MISTRAL_API_KEY\")` raises the same\n`PermissionError`, and `resolve_api_key(\"OPENROUTER_API_KEY\")` succeeds.\n\n**Fix:** `run-vibe.sh` now passes `VIBE_TEST_DISABLE_KEYRING=1` into the sandboxed environment. Vibe's keyring\nmodule honours this switch: `get_api_key_from_keyring` returns `None` without calling `security`. I checked that\n`MISTRAL_API_KEY` then resolves to `None` under the sandbox with no error. I did not loosen `agent.sb`, so the\nKeychain and the real home directory are still unreachable.\n\n**Verification:** with a placeholder `OPENROUTER_API_KEY=dummy-test-key`, the script now gets past startup and fails\nonly at OpenRouter's auth check (`Invalid API key (from env var OPENROUTER_API_KEY)`, exit 1). Startup is fixed. I did\nnot run a real prompt, because `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is not set in the shell I worked in. With your real key set,\n`./run-vibe.sh \"say hi\" /tmp/x` should now run normally.\n\n**Notes:**\n- The stderr text `Reading API keys from the macOS Keychain (...)` in the old log does not appear in the installed\n  Vibe 3.1.0 source. The traceback logic matches, so the log probably came from a slightly different build. The fix\n  holds either way, because the switch is checked before any Keychain read.\n- `VIBE_TEST_DISABLE_KEYRING` is a test-oriented name. It is the only switch I found that stops the Keychain read\n  without changing the installed package or the sandbox. If Vibe is upgraded, check that it still honours it.\n- Alternatives I rejected: allowing `/usr/bin/security` in `agent.sb` (widens the sandbox), or setting a dummy\n  `MISTRAL_API_KEY` (hacky, and it could be sent somewhere). Fixing `_run_security` in the installed package would\n  be the upstream fix, but it is outside this directory.\n- `logs/last-run.out` and `logs/last-run.err` now hold the output of the placeholder-key test run.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017FciNCj4H4ppG176Lkacim","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
