{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsnqqYcaz4show8gh64R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The runs were failing before any model call: Vibe tried to read `MISTRAL_API_KEY` from the macOS Keychain by running `/usr/bin/security`, and the sandbox in `agent.sb` denies that exec. The denial surfaced as an uncaught `PermissionError`, which exits with status 2.\n\n**Fix:** `run-vibe.sh` now passes `VIBE_TEST_DISABLE_KEYRING=1` into the sandboxed environment. Vibe's keyring module honours that switch and skips the Keychain read. The OpenRouter key still comes from `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`. I did not loosen `agent.sb`, and I did not change the installed Vibe package.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Under the same sandbox profile, the Keychain lookup for `MISTRAL_API_KEY` now returns `None` with no error.\n- `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is not set in my shell, so I could not do a real run. With a placeholder key the script now gets past startup and fails only at OpenRouter's auth check (`Invalid API key`, exit 1). With your real key, `./run-vibe.sh \"say hi\" /tmp/x` should run normally. I have not confirmed that end to end.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `run-vibe.sh`: the new env var, plus a comment explaining it.\n- `ANSWER.md`: the cause, the reproduction, the fix, and the notes below.\n- `logs/last-run.out` and `logs/last-run.err` now hold the placeholder-key test output. They are tracked files, so they show as modified.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- The message `Reading API keys from the macOS Keychain` in your old log does not appear in the installed Vibe 3.1.0 code. The traceback still matches, so the log may come from a slightly different build.\n- `VIBE_TEST_DISABLE_KEYRING` is a test-oriented name. If you upgrade Vibe, check that it still honours it.\n- I rejected two alternatives: allowing `security` in the sandbox, which widens it, and setting a dummy `MISTRAL_API_KEY`, which is hacky. The proper upstream fix is for Vibe's `_run_security` to catch `OSError`. That lives outside this directory, so I did not touch it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":641,"cache_read_input_tokens":53810,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":641},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69cb1ba0-5b4a-44ed-a6f2-d183ed56b688","uuid":"5f8808db-5cfd-4ccb-804d-9ada88cd8ff8","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:00:49.344Z","request_id":"req_011CgsnqqMxCB8Q7g794649z"}
